# Raw inputs are not committed: the incident extract is ~1.6 GB across 26 files,
# far past GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit. scripts/fetch_crimes.sh rebuilds it
# from the city's portal and sql/ rebuilds data/derived/ from it.
#
# The community area boundaries are the exception and live in data/derived/:
# the pages fetch that file at runtime, so it has to be committed for the
# published site to work.
data/raw/

# The working DuckDB database, rebuilt by sql/01_load.sql.
data/derived/*.duckdb
data/derived/*.duckdb.wal

# The small aggregates the site actually loads ARE committed, so the published
# pages work from a clean clone with no data pipeline run. They live in
# data/derived/ alongside the database and are listed explicitly in README.md.

node_modules/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.part
